#N canvas 30 30 2700 2200 12;
#X text 20 20 u_state -- the data store \, and the only file that says when state is written. It owns two u_store instances and the state bus \, and knows nothing about what a key means: a contributor names its own key and policy. ref/module/state.md, f 58;
#X text 900 20 creation arg 1: the data DIRECTORY \, absolute and with no trailing slash. inlet 1: a bang meaning RESTORE NOW \, wired from u_init because startup ORDER is u_init's. outlets: none -- everything leaves on the state bus., f 58;
#X text 1560 20 The bus is one name with disjoint selectors \, so there is no loop: contributors send put and route save and restore \, and this file routes put and rejects its own traffic into nothing., f 58;
#X text 20 180 A manual answer must be synchronous: by the time the save broadcast returns every answer is stored \, which is why the write needs no settle timer. A contributor that answers from behind a del is simply missing from the file., f 90;
