#X text 20 890 C-9, f 44;
#X text 320 1820 The directory and both files are made once at load by state-dir.sh \, so a fresh install prints no file errors at boot (ref/module/state.md). On the Mac shell is stubbed \, which is why main-dev.pd passes a directory that exists., f 44;
#X text 900 700 list append forces the selector to list \, so a key named write or load cannot be taken by u_store for a command., f 44;
#X text 1560 900 The commit is right to left: save goes out from the right outlet \, every contributor answers during it \, and only then does the left outlet write the file. Reversed \, the file is one commit stale., f 44;
#X text 2200 620 u_err's shape \, a dirty flag and a metro: capture is unconditional and only the write is rate-limited \, so a burst cannot thrash the SD card. select 1's reject goes nowhere. C-8, f 44;
#X text 320 1240 Restore is manual first \, auto second: if a key is ever in both \, the last replay wins \, and the running value is the more useful., f 58;
#X text 1060 1560 Only the auto store drives the dirty flag: a committed take is written when asked for and at no other time \, which is what lets you abandon one., f 44;
